   }
  ]
 }
];
---

<Layout
  title="How to Win at Word Hunt: Tips and Strategy"
  description="Scoring math, a scanning routine, and two real solved boards. Learn how to find longer words and win more GamePigeon Word Hunt rounds."
  path="/guides/word-hunt-tips"
  ogImage="/images/word-hunt-tips.webp"
  ogImageAlt="A 4x4 Word Hunt board with the path for STRAINED traced across 8 tiles, next to three quick tips"
  ogImageWidth={1200}
  ogImageHeight={720}
  schema={schema}
  ogType="article"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-14 pt-6 sm:px-6 sm:pt-10">
    <header id="top" class="scroll-mt-24">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-4 text-sm text-brand-400 dark:text-brand-300"><a href="/" class="hover:text-headline">Home</a> / <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-headline">Guides</a> / <span aria-current="page">How to Win at Word Hunt</span></nav>
      <div class="grid items-center gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.15fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-10">
      <div>
<h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold leading-[1.15] text-headline dark:text-headline-dark sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem]">How to Win at Word Hunt: Tips and Strategy</h1>
<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-400 dark:text-brand-300">By <a href="/about" class="hover:text-headline">Word Hunt Solver</a> · Published <time datetime="2026-10-06">October 6, 2026</time> · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-08">October 8, 2026</time></p>
<p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Practical habits for finding more words, with two solved boards.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 bg-white shadow-sm dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-800 ">
        <img src="/images/word-hunt-tips.webp" alt="A 4x4 Word Hunt board with the path for STRAINED traced across 8 tiles, next to three quick tips" width="1200" height="720" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="h-auto w-full" />
      </figure>
      </div>
    </header>
    <p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">These Word Hunt tips come from the way the game actually scores. If you want to know how to get better at Word Hunt, start with how the game scores. This guide covers the scoring math, a scanning routine, ways to build longer words, and two real boards we solved, so every tip is backed by numbers. It works the same way whether you play on an iPhone or iPad, since GamePigeon runs inside iMessage on both.</p>
<section id="can-you-win-word-hunt-every-time" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4M7 4h10v5a5 5 0 0 1-10 0V4z"/><path d="M17 5h3v2a3 3 0 0 1-3 3M7 5H4v2a3 3 0 0 0 3 3"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">Can You Win Word Hunt Every Time?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">No. Your opponent might find more words, the board might favor their style, or you might just have an off round. What you can control is how many points you leave on the board. The tips below are about finding more of them, round after round.</p>
</section>
<section id="why-do-long-words-matter-so-much-in-word-hunt" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">Why Do Long Words Matter So Much in Word Hunt?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Word Hunt scores each word by its length, and the points jump fast as words get longer.</p>
<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 shadow-sm dark:border-brand-700"><table class="w-full text-sm"><thead class="bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Word length</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Points</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Same as this many 3 letter words</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-brand-100 dark:divide-brand-700"><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">3 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">100</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">1</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">4 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">400</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">4</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">5 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">800</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">8</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">6 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">1,400</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">14</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">7 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">1,800</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">18</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">8 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">2,200</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">22</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">A single 6 letter word earns more than a dozen 3 letter words. That doesn't mean you should skip short words. It means you should never stop looking for ways to make a word longer.</p>
</section>
<section id="how-do-you-scan-a-word-hunt-board" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">How Do You Scan a Word Hunt Board?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Scanning is how fast your eyes find paths, and it's the core of any good Word Hunt strategy. A steady routine beats staring at random spots.</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">1</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Start From the Center Tiles</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">On a 4x4 board, each of the four center tiles touches 8 others, while a corner tile touches only 3. Words that pass through the center have the most ways to grow, so start there.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">2</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Check Every Direction, Including Diagonals</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">A word can bend up, down, sideways, or diagonally at every step, as long as each letter touches the one before it. Reading only left to right misses every word that runs another way. Trace diagonals on purpose until it becomes a habit.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5 sm:col-span-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">3</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Scan in Zones</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Split a 4x4 board into four corners of 4 tiles each. Clear one zone, then move to the next, then trace paths that cross between zones. Zones keep you from checking the same spot twice and missing another.</p>
<img src="/images/word-hunt-scan-zones.webp" alt="A 4x4 letter grid split into four colored zones of 4 tiles each, numbered 1 to 4" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="mt-4 h-auto w-full rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 dark:border-brand-700" /></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">4</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Match the Shape of a Path, Not Just the Letters</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Once you know where a word sits, think of it as a shape, like an L or a zigzag. Swiping a shape is faster than hunting for each letter while the clock runs.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="which-letters-help-you-most" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1"/><rect x="14" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1"/><rect x="3" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="1"/><rect x="14" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="1"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">Which Letters Help You Most?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Every letter in Word Hunt scores the same, so a Q or a Z earns no more than an E. What matters is how many words a letter helps you build. Common letters like E, A, R, T, N, S, I, and O appear in many English words, so tiles with these letters are where most paths live.</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Vowels are the glue. A consonant with two or three vowels around it can usually start several words. A cluster of consonants with no vowel nearby is often a dead end, so don't waste seconds there. Rare letters like Q, X, J, and Z can still help, as OUTBOX shows in the example below, but check them quickly and move on if nothing appears.</p>
</section>
<section id="longer-words" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">How Do You Find Longer Words?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Long words rarely jump out at you. You build them from words you've already found.</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">1</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Build From a Base Word</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">When you find a short word, treat it as a starting point. Check every tile touching its first and last letters for letters that could extend it.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">2</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Add Prefixes and Suffixes</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Try RE, UN, and DE before a base word, and S, ED, ER, and ING after it. Our <a href="/guides/word-hunt-cheat#cheat-sheet" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">Word Hunt cheat sheet</a> lists more patterns. RAIN can become RAINS, RAINED, or TRAIN when the letters touch. Each version is a new word with its own points.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">3</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Follow Word Families</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">One good word often has relatives nearby. TONE can lead to TONES, TONED, and STONE if the letters connect. When you find a word with a family, check each relative before moving on.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5 sm:col-span-2"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">4</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Look for Smaller Words Inside Longer Ones</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">One swipe can hold several words. The path for STARE also holds STAR, TARE, TAR, and ARE.</p>
<img src="/images/words-inside-stare.webp" alt="The path for STARE on a letter grid, with STAR, TARE, TAR, and ARE found along the same swipe" width="1200" height="700" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="mt-4 h-auto w-full rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 dark:border-brand-700" /></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="worked-example" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.4 15a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 .3 1.8l.1.1a2 2 0 1 1-2.8 2.8l-.1-.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.8-.3 1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1 1.5V21a2 2 0 1 1-4 0v-.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.1-1.5 1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.8.3l-.1.1a2 2 0 1 1-2.8-2.8l.1-.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 .3-1.8 1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.5-1H3a2 2 0 1 1 0-4h.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.5-1.1 1.7 1.7 0 0 0-.3-1.8l-.1-.1a2 2 0 1 1 2.8-2.8l.1.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.8.3H9a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1-1.5V3a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1 1.5 1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.8-.3l.1-.1a2 2 0 1 1 2.8 2.8l-.1.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-.3 1.8V9a1.7 1.7 0 0 0 1.5 1H21a2 2 0 1 1 0 4h-.1a1.7 1.7 0 0 0-1.5 1z"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">A Worked Example: What One Board Really Holds</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">We ran this 4x4 board through our solver:</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid w-56 gap-1.5" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0,1fr));" role="img" aria-label="Word Hunt board: F T U E / V X B O / Z O L P / D B I D"><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">F</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">T</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">U</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">E</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">V</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">X</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">B</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">O</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">Z</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">O</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">L</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">P</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">D</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">B</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">I</div><div class="flex aspect-square items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-brand-100 bg-white text-lg font-bold text-brand-700 dark:border-brand-700 dark:bg-brand-900 dark:text-white">D</div></div>
<img src="/images/word-hunt-example-board.webp" alt="A 4x4 Word Hunt board with the path for OUTBOX traced across six tiles, next to totals of 50 words and 17,100 points" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="mt-4 h-auto w-full rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 dark:border-brand-700" />
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">The solver found 50 words worth 17,100 points in total:</p>
<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 shadow-sm dark:border-brand-700"><table class="w-full text-sm"><thead class="bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Word length</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Words found</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Points</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-brand-100 dark:divide-brand-700"><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">3 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">25</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">2,500</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">4 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">18</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">7,200</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">5 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">4</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">3,200</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">6 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">3</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">4,200</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Two things stand out. First, half the words are 3 letters long, but together they earn only about 15% of the points. Second, just 7 words of 5 or 6 letters earn 7,400 points, more than 40% of the total. The three 6 letter words are DIOBOL, DIPLOE, and OUTBOX.</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">OUTBOX shows how a long word bends. It starts on the O at the right end of the second row, moves up to U, left to T, down to B, down and to the left to the O in the third row, then up to X. Six letters, five turns, 1,400 points.</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">The 5 letter words are BILBO, OBOLI, OXLIP, and POLIO. Several of these are rare words. They're in the ENABLE list, but GamePigeon uses its own list, which isn't public, so we can't say whether the game accepts them. When you practice, start with the common words you'll recognize in real games.</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">We also ran a 5x5 board through the solver. It held 123 words worth 57,400 points, led by KYPHOSIS, an 8 letter word worth 2,200 points.</p>
<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 shadow-sm dark:border-brand-700"><table class="w-full text-sm"><thead class="bg-accent-500 text-brand-700 dark:bg-accent-600"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Word length</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Words found on the 5x5 board</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-brand-100 dark:divide-brand-700"><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">3 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">42</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">4 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">49</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">5 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">22</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">6 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">6</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">7 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">3</td></tr><tr class="odd:bg-white even:bg-brand-50/40 dark:odd:bg-brand-900 dark:even:bg-brand-800"><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">8 letters</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">How to Scan This Board Step by Step</h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Start in the center, where X, B, O, and L sit. X is a rare letter, so check it quickly: it gives VOX, LOX, and BOX, then move on. The O, L, and B around it are where the points are. Work that cluster first, then move to the bottom row, where D, B, I, and D connect with the L and P above them to give LID, DIP, PLOD, and BOLD. Finish with the top row, where T, U, and E join the B and O below for TUBE, BOUT, and OUT.</p>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">The 4x4 board also shows how clusters work. The O, L, and B in the middle produce BLOB, LOBO, OBOL, POLO, BOLO, and LOB. Once you spot a cluster like that, stay with it until it runs dry.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="what-quick-habits-help-in-a-short-round" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">What Quick Habits Help in a Short Round?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Not every one of these Word Hunt tips needs weeks of practice. These three habits work in your very next round.</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">1</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Grab Easy 3 Letter Words Without Stopping Your Scan</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Swipe short words as you see them, but keep your eyes moving. Short words keep your score climbing while you look for longer ones.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">2</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Try Plurals Right Away</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">After every word, check for an S touching its last letter. It takes a second and often adds a 4, 5, or 6 letter word.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">3</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Use the Last Seconds Well</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">When time is almost up, stop chasing long words. Swipe every short word and plural you can see. Quick 100 and 400 point words add up in the final seconds.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="how-do-you-practice-word-hunt-between-matches" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">How Do You Practice Word Hunt Between Matches?</h2></div>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">1</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Review the Words You Missed</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">After a match, enter the same board in <a href="/" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">our free solver</a> and compare its list with what you found. Write down one pattern you missed, like a suffix or a diagonal, and look for it next round.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">2</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Train on High Scoring Boards</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Our <a href="/evolver" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">Board Evolver</a> builds high scoring practice boards. Practicing on boards packed with words gives you more clusters to spot in each session.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">3</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Set One Goal per Round</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Pick a single focus, like trying a plural after every word or finding one 6 letter word. One clear goal is easier to build into a habit than five at once.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">4</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Practice With a Friend</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">After each match, open the same board in our solver together and compare who missed what. You'll both learn faster, and it keeps the game fair.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">5</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Track Your Scores</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Write down your score after each match for a week. Seeing your average climb shows which habits are working, and a drop tells you which ones slipped.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">6</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Practice on 4x4 and 5x5 Boards</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Each size has its own feel. A 5x5 board has more tiles to scan, so practice a steady route around the edges and through the middle.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="what-mistakes-should-you-avoid-in-word-hunt" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"/><path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">What Mistakes Should You Avoid in Word Hunt?</h2></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">The most common mistake is a broken path. Every letter has to touch the one before it, and you can't use the same tile twice in one word.</p>
<img src="/images/word-hunt-valid-invalid-path.webp" alt="Two swipe paths on a grid: one valid path through touching tiles, and one invalid path that jumps a tile" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="mt-4 h-auto w-full rounded-2xl border border-brand-100 dark:border-brand-700" />
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Other mistakes cost points too.</p>
<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">1</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Chasing One Word Too Long</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">If a long word isn't coming together in a few seconds, move on. Ten short words are worth more than one long word you never finish.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">2</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Reading Only Left to Right</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Words bend and run backward. If you only read like a book, you'll miss most of the board. Make yourself trace diagonals and reverse paths every round.</p></div>
<div class="card !p-5"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-headline text-sm font-bold text-white dark:bg-headline-dark">3</span><h3 class="text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Sloppy Swipes</h3></div>
<p class="mt-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Lifting your finger one tile early or late turns a real word into a miss. Smooth, steady swipes beat frantic ones, especially on a crowded 5x5 board.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="frequently-asked-questions" class="scroll-mt-24 py-7 sm:py-9">
<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="section-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M9.1 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.8 1c0 2-3 3-3 3M12 17h.01"/></svg></span><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-[1.75rem] dark:text-white">Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div>
<details class="card group mt-3 !p-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-start gap-3 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-900 hover:bg-brand-50/60 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-brand-700/40"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-500 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700">Q</span><span class="flex-1">Is a 5x5 Board easier than a 4x4 Board?</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-5 w-5 flex-none text-gray-600 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 dark:text-gray-300"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p class="px-5 pb-5 pl-[3.75rem] text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">A 5x5 board has 25 tiles instead of 16, so it usually holds more words. In our two demo boards, the 4x4 board held 50 words and the 5x5 board held 123. More words means more chances to score, but also more board to scan.</p></details>
<details class="card group mt-3 !p-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-start gap-3 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-900 hover:bg-brand-50/60 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-brand-700/40"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-500 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700">Q</span><span class="flex-1">How do you beat someone who always wins?</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-5 w-5 flex-none text-gray-600 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 dark:text-gray-300"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p class="px-5 pb-5 pl-[3.75rem] text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Learning how to win at Word Hunt starts with long words. On our example board, just 7 longer words earned over 40% of the points. Then review each board you lose and learn one new pattern from it.</p></details>
<details class="card group mt-3 !p-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-start gap-3 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-900 hover:bg-brand-50/60 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-brand-700/40"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-500 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700">Q</span><span class="flex-1">Why are some Word Hunt Boards harder than others?</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-5 w-5 flex-none text-gray-600 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 dark:text-gray-300"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p class="px-5 pb-5 pl-[3.75rem] text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">The letters decide most of it. Boards with plenty of vowels and common letters like E, A, R, S, and T connect into many words. Boards with few vowels, or rare letters like Q, Z, and X, have fewer paths that spell anything.</p></details>
<details class="card group mt-3 !p-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-start gap-3 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-900 hover:bg-brand-50/60 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-brand-700/40"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-500 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700">Q</span><span class="flex-1">Can you find 100 Words on one Board?</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-5 w-5 flex-none text-gray-600 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 dark:text-gray-300"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p class="px-5 pb-5 pl-[3.75rem] text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Sometimes. It depends on the board size and its letters. Bigger boards have more paths, so 5x5 and 6x6 boards pass 100 words more often than 4x4 boards. To count the words on any board, enter it in <a href="/" class="font-semibold text-headline underline-offset-2 hover:underline dark:text-headline-dark">our solver</a> and check the Words Found total.</p></details>
<details class="card group mt-3 !p-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer select-none items-start gap-3 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold text-gray-900 hover:bg-brand-50/60 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-brand-700/40"><span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-none items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-500 text-sm font-bold text-brand-700">Q</span><span class="flex-1">Do Plurals count as new Words?</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 h-5 w-5 flex-none text-gray-600 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180 dark:text-gray-300"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><p class="px-5 pb-5 pl-[3.75rem] text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Yes, when the letters connect. STAR and STARS are two separate words, and each one scores on its own. That's why it pays to check for an S touching the last letter of every word you find.</p></details>
</section>
